# The submission image ships src/, scripts/, config/ and models/ and nothing
# else. Everything below either bloats the image, leaks machine-specific
# paths, or -- in the case of the sample videos and the splits -- would ship
# challenge data inside a container we hand to the organizers.
#
# This file belongs at the ROOT of the build context, beside the Dockerfile.
# containers/build_submission.sh places it there.

.git
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Tests, notebooks and tooling: not needed to answer a question, and pytest is
# not installed in the image.
tests/
tools/
conftest.py
pyproject.toml
*.egg-info/
src/surgvu.egg-info/

# Byte-compiled everything. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE keeps new ones from
# appearing; this keeps stale host-built ones from being copied in.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Job logs and outputs from CHTC runs. logs/ alone is tens of thousands of
# files.
logs/
outputs/
condor/
validate_work/
*_results.json
*_candidates.json

# Data. NONE of this may enter the image: the sample videos are challenge
# material, and the extracted shards are hundreds of GB.
data/
shards/
model_cache/
*.mp4
*.zip
*.sif

# Container build scaffolding -- the image does not need the recipe that built
# it. The Dockerfile itself is exempted below so a `docker build -f Dockerfile`
# from a context assembled by build_submission.sh still finds it.
containers/
!Dockerfile

# Documentation and the perception configs that are not the frozen binding.
docs/
*.md
.venv_scoring/
.apptainer_cache/
.apptainer_tmp/
